B.u6. {"problem": "No fixture or scenario uses the deadline. DR1 has none, and no scenario asks for a decision with a deadline. The new behaviour is never exercised or checked, and the new properties carry no source or rationale of their own.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world fixtures (DR1) and scenarios (a-decision-is-taken-once)", "kind": "other"}
B.u11. {"problem": "deadline is a free-form string with no date type or format. A value like 'soon' or '3/4/26' is accepted, and nothing says what a valid deadline is. The new field also has no source or confirmation of its own. It sits under entries whose source is an unrelated interview quote (L5, 'follow the recommendations for 9 and 10').", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline and request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "other"}
B.u16. {"problem": "No scenario or world fixture exercises the new field. DR1 has no deadline and `request_decision` is never run with one, so nothing checks that a deadline given at request time is stored on the DecisionRequest and visible to the owner. The descriptions of DecisionRequest and `request_decision` also do not mention a deadline, even though the request is that the owner sees it when asked.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world.fixtures DR1, scenarios (a-decision-is-taken-once), DecisionRequest.description and request_decision.description", "kind": "reference"}
B.u1. {"problem": "`deadline` is a free-form `string` with no date type, format or check. Owners can enter 'soon', '11/10' or a date already in the past, and nothing validates it or tells the owner how it is read. The stated goal, a visible date that makes the owner answer in time, is not guaranteed. Neither the DecisionRequest description ('sent to that person's outbox') nor the `request_decision` description says the deadline is shown to the owner, and no effect or handoff delivers it.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline and request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u9. {"problem": "No fixture or scenario uses or exercises the new deadline. The DR1 fixture and the 'a-decision-is-taken-once' scenario never set or check it, so nothing verifies that a request with a deadline is created and keeps the value, or that one without a deadline still works.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: world fixtures DR1 and scenarios", "kind": "other"}
B.u10. {"problem": "The request says the owner sees the deadline when asked, but the change only stores it. request_decision has no effect, notification or outbox delivery that surfaces the field, and no rule or scenario shows or checks it. The object description says requests are sent to the person's outbox, but nothing in the declaration does that. The deadline is therefore stored and never shown, so the stated purpose is not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action request_decision and object DecisionRequest", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u13. {"problem": "Nothing exercises the new field. The DR1 fixture has no deadline and no scenario requests a decision with one. The a-decision-is-taken-once scenario never covers the deadline path, so the change is not checked by the harness.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world.fixtures DR1 and scenarios", "kind": "other"}
B.u5. {"problem": "Authoring's declaration changed (a new property and a new action param) but its version is still 12. The composition still pins interface 1 for authoring, so the change is not marked as a new version.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.authoring.interface", "kind": "other"}
B.u7. {"problem": "The change asks that the owner sees the deadline when the decision is asked. It only adds an optional free-text string field. Nothing declares that the deadline is shown or delivered to the owner: there is no handoff, effect or view. The DecisionRequest description still says it is 'sent to that person's outbox' without mentioning a deadline. The string has no date format or validation, so a value like 'soon' is accepted. Nothing happens once the deadline passes: decide is still allowed and nothing is flagged or escalated. The stated purpose, making owners answer in time, is therefore not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: DecisionRequest.deadline, action request_decision (param deadline), DecisionRequest description", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u14. {"problem": "`deadline` is declared as a free `string` on both the DecisionRequest object and the `request_decision` param. Nothing in the YAML says it is a date, fixes a format, or rejects a value like 'soon'. The stated purpose is 'a visible date', so owners can enter text that cannot be read or compared as a date. A deadline that has passed also has no effect: `decide` has no precondition on it and no rule or invariant mentions it.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, objects.DecisionRequest.properties.deadline and actions.request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u3. {"problem": "The request says the owner sees the deadline when asked, but the change only adds a stored optional field. request_decision has no effect or outbox mechanism that shows the deadline to the owner. Nothing flags a request that is open past its deadline, and no rule or precondition acts on it. The purpose of making the owner answer in time is therefore not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action request_decision and object DecisionRequest (deadline)", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u12. {"problem": "The action's public parameters changed (a new optional param on request_decision) and the object gained a property, but the domain version stays at 12 and the composition still pins interface 1. The change is not recorded as a new declaration or interface version.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.authoring.interface", "kind": "other"}
B.u0. {"problem": "The change adds an optional `deadline` to the DecisionRequest object and to the `request_decision` params, which changes the authoring interface. The domain `version: 12` is not bumped. The composition still pins `interface: 1`, and the fixtures and commits carry interface versions, so consumers and the change check cannot tell the interface changed.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, `version` (and the interface the composition pins for authoring)", "kind": "other"}
B.u2. {"problem": "Nothing exercises the new field. The DR1 fixture and the `a-decision-is-taken-once` scenario never set or check a deadline. No rule or scenario says what happens to an open request after its deadline passes or what the owner sees. The new properties also cite the old interview line (L5), which says nothing about deadlines, so they have no confirmed source.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, world fixtures DR1 / scenarios / DecisionRequest source", "kind": "other"}
B.u8. {"problem": "The declaration changed (a new optional property on DecisionRequest and a new optional param on request_decision), but the domain version is still 12. Interface versions are tracked per commit and pinned by the composition (interface: 1), so the additive interface change is not reflected anywhere.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: version", "kind": "other"}
B.u15. {"problem": "The change adds an optional param to a published action, which changes the Authoring interface, but the domain `version` is still 12 and the composition still pins `interface: 1`. Commit fixtures carry interface versions such as 1.2.0. The interface change is not versioned, so consumers cannot tell it apart from the earlier declaration.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.authoring.interface", "kind": "other"}
B.u4. {"problem": "The deadline is an untyped free string (type: string), so 'tomorrow', '2026-13-45' and an empty string are all accepted. There is no date format or validation. Nothing can compare it to the current date or order requests by it.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline and request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "other"}

