A.u2. {"problem": "request_decision now runs `set target.deadline: params.deadline`, but `deadline` is an optional param. When a caller omits it, the effect assigns a missing value. This may fail the action or write an empty value, so the previously working call with no deadline may break. The effect needs a guard, or `deadline` should only be set when provided.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action request_decision effects", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u19. {"problem": "request_decision always runs `set target.deadline: params.deadline`, but `deadline` is optional. When the owner gives no deadline, the effect reads an absent param. Depending on the kernel this is an error or it writes an empty value. That would break every existing request without a deadline, which was valid before the change.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: actions.request_decision effects", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u16. {"problem": "The deadline is a free-form string with no format or check, and nothing makes the owner see it. The only owner-facing step is the generic request, and the domain has no outbox or notification action, handoff or rule. The stated goal 'the owner sees it when asked' is not backed by anything in the declaration. A deadline that passes also has no effect on decide, so it is purely informational.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: DecisionRequest.deadline, request_decision description", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
